#import "/formatting.typ": *

#recipe(
  title: "Sourdough Beer Bread",
  yield: "1 large loaf",
  refs: <kabc_beer-bread>,
  description: [A great dipping bread.],
)[
  Soaker:
  - 141g King Arthur Rolled Oats #aside[1 1/4 cups]
  - 113mℓ boiling water #aside[1/2 cup]

  Dough:
  - 420g King Arthur Artisan Bread Flour #aside[3 1/2 cups]
  - 255g beer#fn[amber or dark ale preferred] #aside[1 cup plus 2 tbsp.]
  - 227g ripe sourdough starter #aside[1 cup]
  - 1 tsp. SAF Instant Yeast #missing[weight]
  - 21g honey #aside[1 tbsp.]
  - 12g table salt #aside[2 tsp.]
][
  + COMBINE soaker ingredients in medium bowl.
  + COVER and set aside.
  + MIX flour, beer, starter, and yeast, until well combined.#missing[duration & strength]
  + COVER. #pause[30 min.]
  + MIX soaker & remaining ingredients into dough until combined. #pause[3-4 min.
      #missing[strength]]
  + COVER. #pause[30 min.]
  + PERFORM one round of stretch & folds.
  + COVER. #pause[30 min.]
  + SHAPE dough into circle on round surface.
  + COVER. #pause[20 min.]
  + SHAPE into compact boule.
  + FLOUR an 8" Round Brotform.
  + REST boule seam-side up in said Brotform. #pause[1 hour]
  + PREHEAT oven, with Bread Steel on center rack, to 230°C. #pause[30 min.; 450°F]
  + INVERT dough onto Parchment Round.
  + SCORE dough several times.
  + MOVE loaf & parchment onto Bread Steel.
  + BAKE covered. #pause[15 min.]
  + COOL oven to 200°C. #aside[400°F]
  + BAKE uncovered, until dark brown. #pause[25-30 min.]
  + MOVE loaf to wire rack.
  + COOL loaf to room temperature.
]
